    card title "Which is heavier?"

Which is heavier? Three pairs, and in each one your eyes may fool you.
    draw heavy

    ask "Which is heavier? Tap the heavier one in each pair." on heavy store h feedback.style warm feedback.perfect "A perfect pair of scales." feedback.good "Your scales are nearly calibrated." feedback.poor "These pairs fool almost everyone." feedback.none "Weight hides well. Now you know where."
        right: All {h} right.
        wrong: {h} right. Here are the weights.

    hide heavy heavy_v_1 heavy_v_2 heavy_v_3 heavy_v_4 heavy_v_5 heavy_v_6 heavy_1 heavy_2 heavy_3 heavy_4 heavy_5 heavy_6 heavy_title

A blue whale's heart is the biggest heart on Earth, yet the one in a Toronto museum weighs about a hundred and eighty kilos. A small car weighs five times as much.
    draw bal1

    erase bal1

But the air in a bedroom outweighs a ten-year-old. Each cubic metre weighs over a kilo, and a bedroom holds about forty.
    draw bal2 air_t

    erase bal2 air_t

And a puffy summer cloud, a kilometre across, holds about five hundred tonnes of water: more than a fully loaded jumbo jet.
    draw bal3 cl_t

So why doesn't it fall? Its droplets are so tiny that rising warm air holds them up.
    highlight b3_l_name b3_l_val

Weight hides in things spread thin: air and mist feel like nothing, but there is a lot of them.
    highlight b3_beam

Next time a cloud drifts by, picture a jumbo jet's worth of water floating over your head.
    highlight b3_l_val effect circle
